# Feature structure & Query

## Features

- Domain code lives in `src/features/<kebab-name>/`
- Keep `src/app/` routes thin: read params, render the feature screen
- Shared UI stays in `src/components/`, shared hooks in `src/hooks/`
- Add a subfolder only when a file needs it. No empty `api/` / `types/` / `docs/`, no barrel `index.ts` for integration

## Query = persisted state (local or remote)

SQLite, files, and HTTP are the same kind of state: they live outside the component tree. Use TanStack Query. `useState` / Context are for UI and session-only client state.

- `queryFn` / `mutationFn` may call a local repository, not only HTTP
- Do not copy Query results into Context
- After a write, `invalidateQueries` (or `setQueryData`) so other screens stay in sync
- Local-only data mutated by this app: `staleTime: Infinity` plus invalidate on write is enough

```ts
// ✅ local DB is still Query
const { data } = useQuery({
  queryKey: ['stamps'],
  queryFn: () => stampRepository.list(),
  staleTime: Infinity,
});
```
